# __PACKAGE_NAME__

An [MDP](https://github.com/barmoshe/mdp) **artifact** extension: a new output
form (alongside the core `page`, `slides`, and `flyer`).

> Scaffolded with `create-mdp-extension`. This starter renders the IR as a single
> centered card; edit `src/index.mjs` to make it your own layout.

## Try it

```sh
npm test          # full-document output, escaping, the design lock, determinism
npm run demo      # writes dist/preview.html - open it in a browser
```

Zero dependencies: it runs anywhere Node 18+ does.

## What an artifact is

An artifact is a solver over the whole IR. It takes `{ meta, blocks }` and returns
a complete, standalone HTML document:

```js
import { __RENDER_FN__ } from "__PACKAGE_NAME__";
import { parse } from "@mdp/core"; // the public parser

const html = __RENDER_FN__(parse(source));
```

The starter handles `title`, `lead`, `paragraph`, `heading`, `list`, and `quote`;
unknown blocks are skipped, mirroring the core renderers' graceful degradation.

## Publish (the convention)

MDP discovers extensions with no central registry - just npm + GitHub search:

1. Keep `"keywords": ["mdp", "__KEYWORD__"]` in `package.json` (already set).
2. `npm publish`
3. Add the **`__KEYWORD__`** topic to the GitHub repo.

It's then found by `npm search keywords:__KEYWORD__` and GitHub's `__KEYWORD__`
topic page.

## Use it in a document

`@mdp/core` has no runtime plugin loader yet. An artifact is invoked directly as
`__RENDER_FN__(parse(source))`, or wired into a fork of
[`@mdp/core`](https://github.com/barmoshe/mdp) as a new entry in the `RENDERERS`
map so the CLI and playground can target it by name:

```js
import { __RENDER_FN__ } from "__PACKAGE_NAME__";
// in packages/core/src/index.mjs:
export const RENDERERS = {
  page: renderPage,
  slides: renderSlides,
  flyer: renderFlyer,
  __SLUG__: __RENDER_FN__,
};
```

## Note on `_tokens.mjs`

The starter vendors a minimal `src/_tokens.mjs` so the document is styled without
an `@mdp/core` install. When `@mdp/core` is published, delete it and
`import { baseStyle } from "@mdp/core"` for the full themed design system.

